# Magic Cabinet — Data Model

> The spec IS the layout engine. Rooms contain walls. Walls have obstacles and hold cabinets. Cabinets use materials. Events drive state transitions. Every entity and relationship is encoded so an AI can simulate: will this layout fit?

---

## Entities

### Entity: Room

A physical kitchen space defined by wall segments. One room per project.

```yaml
entity: Room
type: entity
properties:
  id:
    type: string
    format: uuid-v4
    required: true
  name:
    type: string
    required: true
    constraints: 1-100 chars, non-empty
  wall_count:
    type: number
    required: true
    default: 4
    constraints: 3-8, integer
states: [draft, measured, validated, locked]
lifecycle: draft → measured → validated → locked
```

### Entity: Wall

A single wall segment with dimensions and obstacles. Cabinets are placed on walls.

```yaml
entity: Wall
type: entity
properties:
  id:
    type: string
    format: uuid-v4
    required: true
  length:
    type: number
    required: true
    constraints: ">0, <=20000, mm, integer"
  height:
    type: number
    required: true
    constraints: "2000-3500, mm, integer"
  is_load_bearing:
    type: boolean
    required: true
    default: false
states: [blank, has_obstacles, has_cabinets]
lifecycle: blank → has_obstacles → has_cabinets
```

### Entity: Obstacle

Something on a wall that blocks cabinet placement — windows, doors, outlets, pipes, vents, appliances, sinks.

```yaml
entity: Obstacle
type: entity
properties:
  id:
    type: string
    format: uuid-v4
    required: true
  type:
    type: enum
    values: [window, door, outlet, pipe, vent, structural, appliance, sink, custom]
    required: true
  position_from_left:
    type: number
    required: true
    constraints: ">=0, <=wall.length, mm"
  width:
    type: number
    required: true
    constraints: ">0, <=wall.length, mm"
  height_from_floor:
    type: number
    required: true
    constraints: ">=0, <=wall.height, mm"
  height:
    type: number
    required: true
    constraints: ">0, <=wall.height, mm"
states: [active, removed]
lifecycle: active → removed
```

### Entity: Cabinet

A single cabinet placed on a wall. Widths are discrete (50mm increments). Depth and height determined by type.

```yaml
entity: Cabinet
type: entity
properties:
  id:
    type: string
    format: uuid-v4
    required: true
  type:
    type: enum
    values: [base, wall, tall, corner, sink_base, appliance_garage, open_shelf, custom]
    required: true
  width:
    type: number
    required: true
    constraints: "150-1200, step 50, mm"
  depth:
    type: number
    required: true
    constraints: "base/wall/tall=600, sink_base=650, corner=650, mm"
  height:
    type: number
    required: true
    constraints: "base=720, wall=900, tall=2100, mm"
  material_id:
    type: string
    required: true
    constraints: references Material.id
  position_from_left:
    type: number
    required: false
    constraints: ">=0, mm"
states: [proposed, confirmed, installed]
lifecycle: proposed → confirmed → installed
```

### Entity: Material

A cabinet material/finish combination. Tracks cost, lead time, and stock status.

```yaml
entity: Material
type: entity
properties:
  id:
    type: string
    required: true
    constraints: kebab-case, unique
  name:
    type: string
    required: true
    constraints: 1-100 chars
  type:
    type: enum
    values: [wood, laminate, thermofoil, acrylic, metal, glass, custom]
    required: true
  cost_per_linear_meter:
    type: number
    required: true
    constraints: ">0, USD, 2 decimal places"
  lead_time_days:
    type: number
    required: true
    constraints: ">=0, integer"
  in_stock:
    type: boolean
    required: true
    default: true
states: [available, low_stock, backordered, discontinued]
lifecycle: available → low_stock → backordered → discontinued
```

### Entity: Door

A cabinet door/face — what the customer sees. Tall cabinets can have 2+ doors.

```yaml
entity: Door
type: entity
properties:
  id:
    type: string
    format: uuid-v4
    required: true
  cabinet_id:
    type: string
    required: true
    constraints: references Cabinet.id
  style:
    type: enum
    values: [shaker, slab, raised_panel, glass_front, beadboard, louvers, custom]
    required: true
  hinge_side:
    type: enum
    values: [left, right]
    required: true
  handle_type:
    type: enum
    values: [knob, pull, cup, touch_latch, none]
    required: true
  handle_finish:
    type: enum
    values: [brushed_nickel, chrome, matte_black, brass, bronze, copper, custom]
    required: true
states: [attached, removed, damaged]
lifecycle: attached → removed → attached
```

### Entity: Interior

What's inside the cabinet — shelves and drawers.

```yaml
entity: Interior
type: entity
properties:
  id:
    type: string
    format: uuid-v4
    required: true
  cabinet_id:
    type: string
    required: true
    constraints: references Cabinet.id
  shelf_count:
    type: number
    required: true
    default: 1
    constraints: ">=0, <=5, integer"
  shelf_adjustable:
    type: boolean
    required: true
    default: true
  drawer_count:
    type: number
    required: true
    default: 0
    constraints: ">=0, <=4, integer, base cabinets only"
  soft_close:
    type: boolean
    required: true
    default: false
states: [empty, configured, installed]
lifecycle: empty → configured → installed
```

### Entity: MeasurementSource

How the wall was measured — affects confidence in dimensions.

```yaml
entity: MeasurementSource
type: entity
properties:
  id:
    type: string
    format: uuid-v4
    required: true
  wall_id:
    type: string
    required: true
    constraints: references Wall.id
  method:
    type: enum
    values: [laser, tape, photo_estimate, professional, unknown]
    required: true
  measured_by:
    type: string
    required: true
  measured_at:
    type: datetime
    format: iso8601
    required: true
  photo_url:
    type: string
    format: url
    required: false
states: [submitted, verified, disputed]
lifecycle: submitted → verified → disputed
```

---

## Relationships

### Relationship: Room → Wall

```yaml
relationship: Room → Wall
verb: contains
cardinality: 1:N
required: true
cascade: delete
invariants:
  - room.wall_count === count(walls in room)
```

### Relationship: Wall → Obstacle

```yaml
relationship: Wall → Obstacle
verb: has
cardinality: 1:N
required: false
cascade: delete
invariants:
  - obstacle.position_from_left + obstacle.width <= wall.length
```

### Relationship: Wall → Cabinet

```yaml
relationship: Wall → Cabinet
verb: holds
cardinality: 1:N
required: false
cascade: delete
invariants:
  - sum(cabinet.width for cabinets on wall) + sum(gaps) <= wall.length - sum(obstacle.width for obstacles on wall)
```

### Relationship: Cabinet → Material

```yaml
relationship: Cabinet → Material
verb: uses
cardinality: N:1
required: true
cascade: restrict
invariants:
  - Cannot delete material if any cabinet uses it
```

### Relationship: Cabinet → Door

```yaml
relationship: Cabinet → Door
verb: has
cardinality: 1:N
required: false
cascade: delete
invariants:
  - Tall cabinets can have 2+ doors. Base/wall cabinets typically 1.
```

### Relationship: Cabinet → Interior

```yaml
relationship: Cabinet → Interior
verb: contains
cardinality: 1:1
required: false
cascade: delete
invariants:
  - Drawer count constrained to base cabinets only
```

### Relationship: Wall → MeasurementSource

```yaml
relationship: Wall → MeasurementSource
verb: documented_by
cardinality: 1:1
required: true
cascade: delete
invariants: []
```

---

## Events

### Event: wall.measured

Triggered when user submits wall dimensions. Moves wall from blank to measured. If all walls in room are measured, room state advances to measured.

```yaml
event: wall.measured
trigger: User submits wall dimensions
payload:
  wall_id: string
  length: number (mm)
  height: number (mm)
preconditions:
  - wall.state === blank
postconditions:
  - wall.state === measured
  - wall.length is set
  - wall.height is set
side_effects:
  - room.state → measured (if all walls measured)
probability: null (deterministic)
```

### Event: cabinet.placed

Triggered by layout engine or manual placement. Validates no overlaps with obstacles or other cabinets.

```yaml
event: cabinet.placed
trigger: Layout engine or manual placement assigns cabinet to wall position
payload:
  cabinet_id: string
  wall_id: string
  position_from_left: number (mm)
  width: number (mm)
preconditions:
  - wall.state === has_obstacles
  - position_from_left + width <= wall.length
  - no overlap with any obstacle on wall
  - no overlap with any other cabinet on wall
postconditions:
  - cabinet.state === proposed
side_effects:
  - wall.state → has_cabinets (if first cabinet on wall)
probability: null
```

### Event: material.backordered

Triggered externally when supplier reports stock depletion. Flags all cabinets using this material for review. Extends project timeline.

```yaml
event: material.backordered
trigger: Supplier reports stock depletion
payload:
  material_id: string
  new_lead_time_days: number
preconditions:
  - material.state !== discontinued
postconditions:
  - material.state === backordered
  - material.in_stock === false
  - material.lead_time_days === new_lead_time_days
side_effects:
  - All cabinets using this material flagged for review
  - Project timeline extended by new_lead_time_days
probability: 0.03 (per material, per week)
```

### Event: layout.validated

Triggered when all constraints pass automated check. Room advances to validated state.

```yaml
event: layout.validated
trigger: All constraints pass automated check
payload:
  room_id: string
preconditions:
  - All walls in room have length and height
  - All cabinets have material assigned
  - No cabinet-obstacle overlaps
  - All cabinet widths are valid discrete values
  - All materials are in_stock or backordered (not discontinued)
postconditions:
  - room.state === validated
probability: null
```
